  "result": "I fixed it in `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py`. The direction sign was inverted, so clamping an open bound moved the value the wrong way. It returned `bound - dir` instead of `bound + dir`.\n\nFor example, `IntRange(min=0, min_open=True, clamp=True)` given `-5` returned `-1`, which is outside the range. It now returns `1`. The same applies to `max_open`.\n\n`tests/test_types.py` passes (41 passed, 2 skipped). I didn't add a test for this case.\n\nOne case I left alone: if both bounds are open and adjacent, such as `min=0, max=1`, no integer is valid, so clamping can't produce an in-range value.",
